\newlabel{app:A4}{{}{49}{Appendix A4. Data flow}{section*.69}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {R10}{\ignorespaces Figure\nobreakspace  {}R10.\nobreakspace  Data flow of the image-analysis arm. All counts are images. The training, validation and internal-test sets were drawn from TN3K, TN5K, ThyroidXL and PKTN; the validation set was used to select checkpoints, fit the router and set the referral thresholds, which were then frozen for testing. The external-test cohorts were not used for model development. ZJH-8K served as an external test set for classification and segmentation, whereas its malignant primary lesions were split at the patient level to develop (with five-fold cross-validation) and test the LNM and FTC/PTC models.\relax }}{49}{figure.caption.70}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig_rep_flow_image}{{R10}{49}{\responsefiguretitle {fig_rep_flow_image}{Data flow of the image-analysis arm. All counts are images. The training, validation and internal-test sets were drawn from TN3K, TN5K, ThyroidXL and PKTN; the validation set was used to select checkpoints, fit the router and set the referral thresholds, which were then frozen for testing. The external-test cohorts were not used for model development. ZJH-8K served as an external test set for classification and segmentation, whereas its malignant primary lesions were split at the patient level to develop (with five-fold cross-validation) and test the LNM and FTC/PTC models.}\relax }{figure.caption.70}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {R11}{\ignorespaces Figure\nobreakspace  {}R11.\nobreakspace  Data flow of the report-generation arm. For the auxiliary tools, SMU-HMC data are counted in reports and the other datasets in images (frames for TGVideo); the training, validation and test splits of each tool are given in Supplementary Table S13. The SMU-HMC template library was built from reports with a completeness score of at least 0.9. The KMVE library excluded 406 training reports that were near-duplicates of test reports, and its rules were checked on the validation split. ZJH-TS reports were generated with the SMU-HMC library. The yellow safety rules were selected on the agent's reports for the three test sets and evaluated on TNVideo.\relax }}{50}{figure.caption.71}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig_rep_flow_report}{{R11}{50}{\responsefiguretitle {fig_rep_flow_report}{Data flow of the report-generation arm. For the auxiliary tools, SMU-HMC data are counted in reports and the other datasets in images (frames for TGVideo); the training, validation and test splits of each tool are given in Supplementary Table S13. The SMU-HMC template library was built from reports with a completeness score of at least 0.9. The KMVE library excluded 406 training reports that were near-duplicates of test reports, and its rules were checked on the validation split. ZJH-TS reports were generated with the SMU-HMC library. The yellow safety rules were selected on the agent's reports for the three test sets and evaluated on TNVideo.}\relax }{figure.caption.71}{}}
